 "sources": {
  "davis2020": "GSE116969 dataTable3: driver-line samples grouped by type (250 samples; 16 mock, no-driver, bead and Tm1 protocol controls excluded); mean log1p(TPM)",
  "ozel2021": "GSE142787 Adult sheet: published log-normalised cluster averages",
  "davie2018": "GSE107451 57k whole brain: mean log1p(cp10k) and detection fraction per annotation; reproduces flybrain's expression_central.csv to rounding",
  "afca2023": "GSE218661 Aging Fly Cell Atlas head: mean of the published log1p(cp10k) and detection fraction per afca_annotation (all ages and sexes)",
  "adfca2025": "GSE261656 AD Fly Cell Atlas head, control samples: umi_counts -> log1p(cp10k) per adfca_annotation",
  "not_used": "D3 Kurmangaliyev 2020 (matrix not downloaded; Ozel covers the adult optic lobe); D5 lineage route (see lineage)"
 },
 "tiers": "flybrain type maps (exact, alias, fuzzy, class); best tier per cell, then source order davis2020 > ozel2021 > davie2018 > afca2023 > adfca2025; fca2022 labels applied to both FCA-derived atlases",
 "lineage": "No lineage tier (M2): Allen et al. 2026 (D5) Tables S2-S5 name central-brain types by transmitter (Achl_000 ...) and carry no hemilineage labels, so the planned route Allen type -> hemilineage -> itoleeHl cannot be built (manuscript/SINGLE_CELL_T-SC0_SEARCH.md). The approved fallback applies: the central brain stays at class level. The adult VNC atlas (Allen et al. 2020, GSE141807) gives hemilineages per cluster only (eLife source data; no per-cell labels deposited) and would reach at most the VNC share of the trace carriers (about 45%), below the gate; it is not used.",
